course: dictionary
lesson: 2655
title: Scripts and writing systems
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A script is a set of letters or symbols used to write a language. Languages do not all share one script. English uses the Latin alphabet, but other languages use different letters. «Languages are written in different scripts, such as the Latin alphabet, Cyrillic (used for Russian), Arabic, Devanagari and Chinese characters, and Serbian can be written in both Cyrillic and Latin letters.» The sentence shows that the same language can even use more than one script.
explain: Devanagari is one script. It is used to write Hindi, Marathi, Nepali, Sanskrit and several other languages of India and Nepal. You can spot Devanagari by the straight line along the top, which the letters hang from. Like English, it is written from left to right.
explain: When you see a word written in an unfamiliar script, you cannot read it yet, even if you know the language it is written in. Look for clues: the shape of the letters, a line along the top, or the words around it. Then ask a teacher or use a dictionary to find out which script it is.
fact: A script is a set of letters or symbols used to write a language.
fact: Devanagari is a script, not a language.
fact: Devanagari is used for Hindi, Marathi, Nepali and Sanskrit, among others.
fact: Devanagari letters hang from a straight line along the top.
fact: Devanagari is written from left to right, like English.
exercise: «Languages are written in different scripts, such as the Latin alphabet, Cyrillic (used for Russian), Arabic, Devanagari and Chinese characters.» Which language is written in Devanagari? | *Hindi | Japanese | English | Russian
exercise: Which way is Devanagari written? | *Left to right | Right to left | Top to bottom | Bottom to top
exercise: What is Devanagari? | A type of music | *A writing system (script) | A kind of food | A country in Asia
exercise: Which script is used for Russian? | Devanagari | Latin | *Cyrillic | Arabic
exercise: Ella says Devanagari and Cyrillic are both languages. Is she right? | Yes, Devanagari is a language and Cyrillic is a country | No, neither is used for writing | Yes, both are languages | *No, both are scripts, and Hindi and Russian are languages
exam: Serbian «can be written in both Cyrillic and Latin letters.» What does this sentence show about scripts? | *A language can be written in more than one script | Latin letters are only used for English | A language can only ever be written in one script | Cyrillic letters are only used for numbers
